ppu_lifter: --probes FILE, a diagnostic call to the host at chosen instruction addresses.

Overrides (--overrides) only replace whole functions; a loop inside one function cannot be watched from its entry.
With --probes, every listed instruction address gets `ppu_probe(ctx, addr)` emitted right before its lifted line
(after its label, if any), with the guest registers as they are before that instruction. The declaration is at
block scope (C++ linkage) so the shared header and the other chunks are unchanged; the host defines ppu_probe.
The parallel lift (-j) hands the list to its workers like the other lift context.
Without --probes (the default) the output is byte-identical.

Use: watching the loop of Killzone 2's AI waypoint search (0x613DF0) from inside.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (hand-merged): lifter probes beside upstream's insn_patches (_worker_init(..., toc_base=0, insn_patches=None, probes=None))

